From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] web: a busy cursor while a timing report is built
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Qt GUI shows a wait cursor while it builds the timing report a click
on a slack-histogram bucket asks for. The web viewer showed nothing: on
a large design (XiangShan's tile, 2.7 M instances) the report takes
seconds, and the click looks ignored.

withBusyCursor() (ui-utils.js) puts a progress cursor on the whole page,
the map included, while a request runs; it is counted, so overlapping
requests keep it until the last one ends, and cleared when the request
fails. Used by the bucket click, the fanout/net-length bin double-click
and the timing widget's Update.
---
